Z||000000||SteveJ||03-05-2001||01:30 PM||||I have a 3800 auto but it needs its second gear repaired. I think it needs a band but a repair manual would be good before I open it.<P> So do you think this book by Haynes covers it? ( noting that the 4T60 is an update of the 440 and it looks like the book covers 400 series transmissions ) You know how these books come wrapped in celophane today you can't really get a good look at 'em.<BR> <BR>10360 - General Motors Automatic Transmission Overhaul Manual Written to the same style as the Ford manual described above. A must for the serious GM do-it-yourselfer. Covers THM 2004R, 350, 400 and 700R4 automatic transmissions.<P><BR>Anybody know any good sites on Auto trans repairs?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||03-05-2001||04:31 PM||||That book only covers the RWD models. JC Whitney carries ATSG manuals, I used one for a 700R4 rebuild. It was a good manual and even gives part #s and recomendations for parts that should be upgraded. They have manuals for the 4T60 and the 4T60E transmissions.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 03-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-05-2001||09:36 PM||||I don't remember if they have manuals or not. they have all the parts. <A HREF="http://www.txchange.com/" TARGET=_blank>Transmission Exchange Co.</A> You may as well get a whole rebuild kit for it while it's out. No sense fixing just one part.||||reg||1
